  "entity_raw": {
    "name_raw": "Shifting Patterns",
    "definition_type_raw": null,
    "source_book_raw": "Distant Realms pg. 42",
    "definition_raw": "Source Distant Realms pg. 42\nYou can focus your concentration when maintaining pattern effects to slowly move them.\n\nPrerequisites: Spell Focus (illusion), caster level 5th.\n\nBenefit: When you are concentrating to maintain a spell from the pattern subschool, you can move any area effects associated with that spell by up to 10 feet as a move action. Creatures within the new area of effect are subject to the spell as if it had just been cast (attempting saves as normal). When concentrating on a pattern spell that already allows you to move the effect, such as rainbow pattern, increase the distance you can move the pattern by 50%.",
